#91750
"Small Dark Cave"
"This small limestone cave stands about eight feet in height at its tallest,

just high enough to accommodate a full-sized ogre, and digs roughly twelve feet

into the side of the mountain.  Dry and dusty, the ground is mostly comprised

of packed dirt and gravel, with patches of weed-ridden grass growing as you

approach the mouth of the cave to the east.  On the west end, steeped in shadow,

lies the boarded-up entrance to a vertical mine shaft.

"
"<pry boards> to gain entrance (needs crowbar)

<break/kick/bash boards> to gain entrance (str check)

---

[Semix] Maybe add leaving (down) acode.

[Semix] Need a copy of acode 5 (leaving trigger) put in the room east (for Kotoktok)

"
33030156 0
11 5 0
D1
""
""
0 -1 57288 20 5
D5
"mine shaft"
"mine shaft"
8419 -1 91751 0 5
A
"pry"
"d do down boards"
"if( !is_open( room, down ) ) {

  if( has_obj( 241, ch ) ) {

   act_tochar( #pry, ch );

   act_notchar( #rpry, ch );

   open( room, down );

  }

  else

    act_tochar( #nobar, ch );

}

else

  act_tochar( #opened, ch );

"
E
"opened"
"The boards have already been removed.

"
E
"pry"
"@yYou pry the boards loose, exposing the dusty entrance to a steeply inclined

mine shaft.@n

"
E
"rpry"
"@y$n pries the boards loose, exposing the dusty entrance to a steeply inclined

mine shaft.@n

"
E
"nobar"
"You aren't carrying anything that can pry the boards loose.  Perhaps you

should try a crowbar.

"
!
0 0 0
A
"break kick punch bash"
"d do down boards"
"if( !is_open( room, down ) ) {

  if( find_stat( ch, str ) > 15 ) {

   act_tochar( #break, ch );

   act_notchar( #rbreak, ch );

   open( room, down );

  }

  else

    act_tochar( #weak, ch );

    act_notchar( #rweak, ch );

}

else

  act_tochar( #opened, ch );

"
E
"opened"
"The boards have already been removed.

"
E
"break"
"@yYou furiously attack the boards, sending pieces of wood flying and exposing

the dusty entrance to a steeply inclined mine shaft.@n

"
E
"rbreak"
"@y$n furiously attacks the boards, sending pieces of wood flying and exposing

the dusty entrance to a steeply inclined mine shaft.@n

"
E
"weak"
"@cYou throw your weight against the boards, but are unable to do more than send

dust flying.@n

"
E
"rweak"
"@c$n throws $s weight against the boards, but is unable to do more than send

dust flying.@n

"
