#91787
"Vertical Mine Shaft"
"This vertical mine shaft leads both up and down via a series of iron rungs,

secured by steel spikes driven into the side of the limestone shaft.  Above

leads toward a barely visible exit, though it is impossible to tell if the

way is clear from here. As the passageway continues further down, the

limestone gives way to solid granite, with flecks of glittering quartz

embedded into the surface of the chiseled walls.  Sturdy beams of that same,

hard stone brace walls just wide enough to squeeze an large ogre through.

"
""
